---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="ABA Centers | Carlos Menco Guardo" mainClass="main-content main-content--project-detail" activePage="abacenters" pageScripts={["/js/project-scroll-gradient.js"]}>
  <div class="content--sidebar">
    <div class="project-header">
      <div class="project-img-wrapper">
        <img src="/imgs/abacenters-thumb.svg" alt="ABA Centers redesign preview" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="s1">
      <span class="project-detail-year">2026</span>
      <h5 class="project-detail-title">ABA Centers Structural Redesign</h5>
      <p class="project-detail-description">A structural redesign proposal for a therapy services website, using WordPress as a headless CMS and a modern frontend built with Next.js, TypeScript, GSAP, and Tailwind CSS.</p>
      <a href="https://abacenter-front.vercel.app/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="external-link">View prototype <span class="external-link-icon"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M4.22876 4.22924V5.5586L9.49435 5.56332L3.75736 11.3003L4.70017 12.2431L10.4372 6.50613L10.4324 11.7717H11.7712V4.22924H4.22876Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span></a>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Overview</h6>
      <p>ABA Centers is a redesign proposal focused on improving the structure, clarity, and frontend experience of a therapy services website. The concept separates content management from presentation by using WordPress as a headless CMS and a custom Next.js frontend.</p>
      <p>The goal is to create a site that feels more organized, easier to navigate, and more scalable for service content, locations, landing pages, and future marketing needs.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Role</h6>
      <p>Structural redesign, frontend architecture, headless WordPress planning, Next.js and TypeScript development, Tailwind implementation, GSAP interaction planning, and Codex-assisted optimization.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Challenge</h6>
      <p>Therapy websites need to communicate trust, services, eligibility, locations, and next steps with very little friction. The challenge was to propose a cleaner structure while keeping the system flexible enough for content teams and performant enough for a modern marketing site.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Solution</h6>
      <ul>
        <li>Proposed a headless architecture with WordPress managing content and Next.js handling the frontend.</li>
        <li>Used TypeScript and Tailwind CSS for a cleaner, more maintainable interface layer.</li>
        <li>Planned GSAP interactions to make key transitions feel polished without making the site heavy.</li>
        <li>Used Codex to speed up implementation decisions, refactor components, and optimize results.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Outcome</h6>
      <p>The proposal creates a stronger technical and content foundation for a therapy services brand: faster frontend delivery, cleaner content workflows, and a structure that can scale across services and locations.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
